okf_version: "1.0"
knowledge:
  task:
    id: delluhiold-alibaba-latency-diagnosis-20260822
    date: "2026-08-22"
    objective: >-
      Determine from live measurements whether the current slow response speed
      on delluhiold is solely a network problem.

  observed_runtime:
    host: delluhiold
    user: oneciel
    workspace: /home/oneciel/ai-net
    runtime_version: 0.2.22-nightly.20260822-072935.ce72ccc
    provider: alitoken
    model: qwen3.8-max
    effort_level: xhigh
    endpoint_base: >-
      https://token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
    request_observation:
      timestamp_utc: "2026-08-22T07:39:06Z"
      input_tokens_estimated: 82448
      request_bytes: 341027
      messages: 112
      tools: 30
      stream: true

  network_measurement:
    target: token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com
    method: >-
      Five fresh unauthenticated HTTPS requests to the configured OpenAI base;
      HTTP 401 was expected and retained DNS/TCP/TLS/TTFB timing.
    samples_seconds:
      total: [0.750097, 0.734291, 0.742418, 0.755196, 0.740999]
      dns_range: [0.014903, 0.037223]
      tcp_complete_range: [0.248820, 0.268122]
      tls_complete_range: [0.496073, 0.515799]
      ttfb_range: [0.734256, 0.755160]
    result: >-
      A new DNS+TCP+TLS+401 exchange consistently completed in about 0.73 to
      0.76 seconds. Network latency is measurable but does not account for
      multi-second to 49-second model-turn intervals by itself.

  host_measurement:
    load_average: [3.74, 2.18, 1.68]
    cpu_idle_samples_percent: [84, 90, 95, 92, 77]
    memory:
      total: 14GiB
      available: 4.4GiB
      swap_used: 11GiB
    pressure_avg10:
      cpu_some: 2.41
      memory_some: 0.00
      memory_full: 0.00
      io_some: 0.00
      io_full: 0.00
    swap_activity_during_vmstat:
      swap_in_pages_per_second_samples: [4, 0, 0, 0]
      swap_out_pages_per_second_samples: [0, 0, 0, 0]
    result: >-
      Swap occupancy is high, but the measurement window showed no memory or
      I/O pressure and almost no active swap-in. The sampled host state does
      not establish resource pressure as the current response-delay cause.

  transcript_measurement:
    transcript: >-
      /home/oneciel/.claude/projects/-home-oneciel-ai-net/
      bd9b33a6-2be4-46ac-81bc-2bd5c5eed995.jsonl
    definition: >-
      Interval from a recorded local tool_result to the next recorded
      assistant thinking block for the latest 30 tool turns.
    sample_count: 30
    seconds:
      minimum: 4
      median: 6
      p90: 11
      maximum: 49
    long_samples:
      - from_utc: "2026-08-22T07:36:49.808Z"
        to_utc: "2026-08-22T07:37:15.198Z"
        rounded_seconds: 26
        response_output_tokens: 982
      - from_utc: "2026-08-22T07:38:01.633Z"
        to_utc: "2026-08-22T07:38:50.011Z"
        rounded_seconds: 49
        response_output_tokens: 2004
    local_tool_result_observation: >-
      Most recorded tool_use-to-tool_result boundaries were approximately
      0.1 seconds; several shell commands took approximately 1.1 to 1.2
      seconds. The longer delay begins after the tool result and before/during
      the next assistant generation.

  conclusion:
    verified: >-
      The observed slowdown is not solely a network problem. Fresh network
      exchange time was under 0.76 seconds, while model-turn intervals were
      4 to 49 seconds. The longer interval is on the upstream response path
      after a local tool result, with qwen3.8-max configured at xhigh and an
      observed request size of approximately 82K tokens.
    unresolved: >-
      Available telemetry does not separate Alibaba-side queue time, prompt
      ingestion time, and model inference/reasoning time. Therefore no single
      one of those components is asserted as the exact root cause.
    evidence_boundary: >-
      Host resource measurements are a short live sample, and the network
      probe measured an authentication rejection rather than a full model
      generation. Both are sufficient to reject network-only attribution but
      not to assign exact percentages to every latency component.
